            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0139" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7661/10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Wilson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 135.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Beaupré’s dispatch No. 579, of the 3d ultimo, reporting the admission of a
                    shipment of American deviled ham, and expressing the opinion that in future such
                    importations would be attended with no difficulty.</p>
                <p>The department regrets that there has been a renewal of this troublesome
                    question, as shown by your telegram of the 11th [10th] instant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
